a new grindelwald an old call back and a  mysterious absence what do all these  things add up to and do we ever find out  the secrets of dumbledore here are the  best and worst things about fantastic  beasts three  fans have waited for the wizarding world  franchise to officially address  dumbledore's sexuality ever since writer  jk rowling stated that the headmaster  had a love affair with grindelwald in  his youth but with rowling never  offering any canonical confirmation and  two dumbledore grindelwald centric  fantastic beasts prequels having come  and gone fans had begun to think the day  would never come yet at the beginning of  secrets of dumbledore the love affair  between grindelwald and dumbledore is  explicitly confirmed during a dinner  chat with the burgeoning dictator  dumbledore admits that he had previously  gone along with grindelwald because he  was in love with him though the lines  confirming a romantic connection only  amassed about six seconds and were cut  from certain international markets that  might be enough for fans it was you who  said we could reshape the world  but it was our birthright  fans related to see muggle jacob  brandishing a seemingly functional ones  in the film's trailers alas deceptive  editing has struck once again as the  film elaborates that jacob's weapon is  made of snake wood and doesn't even have  a core on one hand it makes far more  sense that jacob isn't a no match born  wizard yet to tap into his powers  however if he had just a teensy bit of  lingering magic from an ancestor it  would explain why he so easily recalled  magical events after getting obliviated  neither harry potter nor fantastic  beasts have explored this possibility  but it makes sense that there are  varying levels of powers in wizards we  already know that some wizards struggle  with spell work while others saw so  who's to say the wrong people with a  dollop of latent magic that can be used  in a pinch but isn't powerful enough to  board the hogwarts express technically  the movies could still explore this down  the line since jacob's wand is a dead to  begin with but overall the bait and  switch is pretty lame  the fantastic beast films gave fans an  adult glimpse at the wizarding world  that offers a different perspective than  what audiences got from the original  movies nevertheless it sure is nice to  come home well the first two fantastic  beasts movies featured hogwarts  minimally secrets of dumbledore  recaptures the unbridled magic from the  harry potter films the adult fandom can  now relive their youth with a nostalgic  homage that doesn't take away from the  plot the movie treats fans to gorgeous  aerial shots of hogwarts filled with  nods to the original series these  moments will transport fans directly  back to their childhood providing  valuable reminders of why this battle is  so important while the fantastic beast  films of adults waging this war against  tyranny rather than children they are  fighting for the future that will give  those children their moment in the sun  there's a certain generational beauty to  that hogwarts will never stop being home  for fans and these reminders of what's  at stake puts the overall battle into  grand perspective  if we're to defeat him you'll have to  trust me  the romanticization of snape and  dumbledore was bad enough in the harry  potter series when harry named his son  albus severus after the bravest men he  ever knew fans know that although both  snape and dumbledore had their moments  stape only turned away from voldemort's  murderous mission after the death of  lily a woman he essentially stalked for  years prior to his redemption snape was  perfectly content to let lily's son and  husband die at the hands of voldemort so  his rebellion against voldemort wasn't  exactly noble he even went on to bully  his supposed love son for seven years  yet despite snape's behavior toward lily  and his selfish obsessive love for her  fans still romanticize the word always  the line references a time when snape  uses his patronus in front of dumbledore  when dumbledore sees that's name's  patronus is still lily's stag he asks  after all this time  [Music]  always  cut to the secrets of dumbledore when  aberforth meets his son credence who  asks did you ever think of me aberforth  says always not only is it an  unnecessary nod to snape but it's also  more proof that aberforth knew about his  son and did little to nothing to find  him  dumbledore and grindelwald are two of  the most compelling mysterious and  utterly confounding characters in the  wizarding world franchise with their  epic plot line that has played out in  these three films it's easy to sometimes  forget that the series is called  fantastic beasts duke scamander and his  little critters often feel like an  afterthought the secrets of dumbledore  brings the creatures back to the  forefront of the story making their  appearances integral to the rapidly  darkening overall storyline harry potter  has always been heavy on mythology and  the chilean's mythos and the secrets of  dumbledore is directly tied to the  film's upcoming election in the new  movie these creatures aid in choosing  the leader of the magical world bowing  to someone worthy of the title while  being integral to the story the  chilean's birth is also a stunning  impactful moment for the franchise as a  whole given that dumbledore was harry's  hero and mentor in the original series  which takes place from the young  wizard's point of view it's only natural  that he would glamorize the headmaster's  behavior however fantastic beasts is an  adult series and it's time to hold  dumbledore accountable for his actions  for starters why is it that after it's  been established many times that  dumbledore should avoid power the  chilean kneels down before him the  chilean bowing to dumbledore and does  all those lessons and feels like pure  fan service given that the movie's title  is secrets of dumbledore it would be  nice if the film honed in on the  mysteries and mistakes of dumbledore  rather than painting him in a flawless  light  both the harry potter and fantastic  beasts movies are inherently political  in nature given that they feature  dictators rising to power yet since the  original series took place at a school  filled with youngsters it prevented fans  from diving too deep into the politics  of it all now with adult characters  hailing from various countries secrets  of dumbledore offers the most in-depth  look yet at wizarding politics and how  an election is held the film explores  ancient rituals for determining new  leaders with such elements as the  introduction of the chileans the movie  also rectifies the second film's mistake  of glamorizing grindelwald with new  quotes that blatantly say in effect  dictators are bad all in all the movie  manages to add a touch of magic to the  politics of the series while honing in  on how a megalomaniac like grindelwald  could manipulate voters and hold an  election hostage luckily newton's merry  band of misfits make grindelwald's reign  as an official leader short-lived this  would have been only the beginning of  grindelwald's reign of terror if by tea  time all of us are still alive  we should consider our efforts a success  the recast from johnny depp to mass  mickelson is striking but it's not just  a change in actor that is glaringly  obvious grindelwald's entire aesthetic  from hair all the way down to his  personality is completely reimagined in  the new film there doesn't even seem to  be any effort to make them feel the same  which will make it difficult to re-watch  the fantastic beasts movies together  someday nevertheless it might be smart  michelson and deb are two extremely  different actors and it seems foolhardy  to ask the former to mimic the latter so  it's refreshing to see mickelson play  the character with more of a simmering  twisted approach than the overt maniacal  way depp approached it the plotline  calls for a charming duplicitous quality  to the dictator for his rise to power to  be believable after all if secrets had  offered a tangible reason for  grindelwald's new appearance however it  would have made the films flow so much  better  magical creatures were the name of the  game in 2016's fantastic beasts and  where to find them the crimes of  grindelwald was a messy mishmash of a  sequel now secrets of dumbledore takes  fans back to what they love most about  the wizarding world franchise the magic  most of the harry potter movies had at  least one epic one wielding duel  particularly in the later installments  secrets does a terrific job escalating  tension as it gets to the big election  and the final battle in its aftermath  the first significant clash between  dumbledore and grindelwald that we've  ever seen on screen witnessing  grindelwald's murder of the chilean  serves as a reminder that he is a  dangerous ruthless man and things  quickly escalate from there not only  does the moment show grindelwald's  murderous impulsivity but it also offers  a glimpse of what grindelwald is truly  capable of when he declares war on the  muggle world grindelwald and  dumbledore's battle results in a spell  vortex for grindelwald and dumbledore  there's an added level of heartbreak  when the pair audibly hear each other's  heartbeats the result is far and away  the most climactic ending to any of the  fantastic beasts films it also carries  with it an appropriate level of heart  magic incredible special effects and a  tease for what's to come  if you check the website does the dog  die before tuning into any movie  involving an animal you're not alone it  can be painful and even triggering to  watch creatures get brutally murdered  even pretend ones with secrets of  dumbledore fans are forced to bear  witness to not one but two savage death  scenes for the angelic deer-like  chileans after newt assists and the  wondrous birth of the chilean twins a  group of grindelwald's minions show up  firing killing curses at them one hits  the mama chillin and we watch her slowly  die as she sees her baby carted off by  the enemy before newt notices her second  baby the heartbeat of the harry potter  franchise has always been a threefold of  love loss and the will to keep fighting  while the ending of the crimes of  grindelwald seemed like it could be a  final nail in the coffin of queenie and  jacob's sweet romance the secrets of  dumbledore reminds fans that almost no  one is beyond saving if they choose to  be better despite queenie's lapse in  judgment when she witnesses  grindelwald's cruelty first hand she can  no longer abide helping him queenies  turn back to the right side of the war  the love she shares with jacob and their  wedding at the end of the film are  exactly what the characters and fans  need to keep fighting for a future of  love and tolerance  corbin tina goldstein has been a staple  of the fantastic beast films from the  very beginning while she's underutilized  in crimes of grindelwald her absence is  even more noticeable in secrets of  dumbledore a handful of scenes she  appears in consist of her simply  reacting to the film's events without  much substance given that she was  promoted to the head of the usara office  off-screen her absence is even more  perplexing it's reasonable to assume  that she would help out with some of the  political uprisings shown throughout the  movie the movie doesn't even have a  throwaway line that tina is on a top  secret assignment either she's just  absent while some fans have guessed that  tina's absence is due to actress  catherine waterstone's unequivocal  criticism of j.k rowling's controversial  comments nothing has been confirmed by  warner brothers as of the making of this  video whether that's the cause or not  it's the movie's job to have tina's  absence make sense plot-wise and in that  respect it really falls short  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

